{2x-5}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{({x}^{2}-{3}^{2}){2}^{2x-5}}{{3}^{2x-5}} & \\ge \\frac{0}{{3}^{2x-5}} \\\\ {x}^{2}-{3}^{2} & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve this inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-{3}^{2} & \\ge 0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & \\ge {3}^{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & \\ge \\sqrt{{3}^{2}} \\\\ |x| & \\ge 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality above is  $x\\le -3$ or $x\\ge 3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-278284/field-1" "q-278284/field-2" "q-278284/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ac76d62e-6bea-515a-af06-e4fae7bc1338"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-278284"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
